<title>JAPAN: Japan April private machine orders up 7.2 pct.</title>
<headline>Japan April private machine orders up 7.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's private-sector machinery orders, excluding those for machinery at electric power firms and for ships, rose a seasonally adjusted 7.2 percent in April from the previous month to 1.09 trillion yen, the Economic Planning Agency (EPA) said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>Month-on-month percentage changes, seasonally adjusted, in different categories of machinery orders were as follows:</p>
<p>			 APR	     MAR</p>
<p>Overall	     +2.0	    -1.7</p>
<p> Private	    +7.2	   -12.7</p>
<p>(excluding ships, electric utilities)</p>
<p> Public	     -3.1	   +31.9</p>
<p> External	  +13.1	    +7.1</p>
<p>Year-on-year percentage changes, not adjusted for seasonal factors, in different categories of machinery orders were as follows:</p>
<p>			 APR	     MAR</p>
<p>Overall	     -1.3	    +6.9</p>
<p> Private	    -6.1	    +0.1</p>
<p>(excluding ships, electric utilities)</p>
<p> Public	     -2.0	   +11.8</p>
<p> External	  +31.8	   +13.9</p>
</text>
